iption":"For a user-requested bounded wait on a resource paths batch only. timeBudgetMs covers the complete operation, including lookup and acquisition; default 30000, maximum 120000. File and byte limits stay unchanged. No automatic retry.","properties":{"timeBudgetMs":{"maximum":120000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["timeBudgetMs"],"type":"object"},"from":{"description":"For an authored relative file link, copy the fixed sr:S/sr:R or canonical skill:// ref of the actual file containing that link. Put the original relative link in path. Nested documents use their own resource ref, not the main Skill ref. Source-backed cross-Skill links resolve through the shared Source mapping; targets keep their own versions. Excludes paths batches and refresh:true.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read","type":"number"},"offset":{"description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)","type":"number"},"path":{"description":"Local file path (relative or absolute), an issued skill:// or sr: ref, or a supplied Notion Skill page URL. Notion main reads inspect without adopting task instructions. Copy refs verbatim; never guess filesystem paths.","type":"string"},"paths":{"description":"Copy complete resource refs verbatim from the selected Skill snapshot's resource directory. Every ref must identify a file in the same owner and snapshot. Reads all selected files in one operation without preparing the main body.","items":{"pattern":"^(?:sr:R[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}|skill:\\/\\/.+)$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"refresh":{"description":"Use only for a user-requested current-version inspection; a successful complete read needs no follow-up refresh. Keeps the active selection unchanged. Only for a supplied Notion Skill ref in path; fixed resources and local files keep their versions.","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\n\nCodemode: `tools.bash(args)` resolves to `{ output, truncated, full_output_path?, exit_code, wall_time_seconds }`.","name":"bash","parameters":{"properties":{"command":{"description":"Shell command to execute","type":"string"},"timeout":{"description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)","type":"number"}},"required":["command"],"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\n\nCodemode: `tools.edit(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"edit","parameters":{"properties":{"edits":{"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.","items":{"properties":{"newText":{"description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit.","type":"string"},"oldText":{"description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.","type":"string"}},"required":["oldText","newText"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","edits"],"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"strict":"prefer","type":"json_schema"},"description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\n\nCodemode: `tools.write(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"write","parameters":{"properties":{"content":{"description":"Content to write to the file","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"],"type":"object"}},{"constrainedSampling":{"type":"grammar","variants":{"openai_lark":"\nstart: options_source | plain_source\noptions_source: OPTIONS_LINE NEWLINE SOURCE\nplain_source: SOURCE\n\nOPTIONS_LINE: /[ \\t]*\\/\\/ @options:[^\\r\\n]*/\nNEWLINE: /\\r?\\n/\nSOURCE: /[\\s\\S]+/\n"}},"description":"Run JavaScript that calls other tools. The input is raw JavaScript (not JSON, no code fence), run as an async function body in a QuickJS sandbox: top-level `await` and `return` work. No Node, file system, network, or timers.\n- `await tools.<name>({ ...args })` resolves to a string, or an object if the tool's declaration says so, and rejects with an Error on failure. A tool whose declaration returns an object resolves on failure too when it returned that object; check its fields. Calls still running when the script ends are cancelled.\n- Optional first line: `// @options: {\"max_output_tokens\": 10000, \"timeout_ms\": 60000}`\n\nGlobals:\n- `text(value)`, `image(dataUrlOrImageBlock)`, `console.log(...)`, and top-level `return` add output; `exit()` ends the script. With several text items, each starts with a `==> text N/M <==` line, and `console` lines follow the other output in one `<console_output>` block. `image()` also saves the image to a temp file and the result names its path.\n- `store(key, value)` and `load(key)` keep JSON values across codemode calls.\n- `ALL_TOOLS`, `await searchTools(query, { limit?, namespace? })`, `await describeTool(name)`, `await describeNamespace(name)`: find unlisted tools, such as MCP tools.","name":"codemode","parameters":{"properties":{"code":{"description":"Raw JavaScript source.","type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"type":"object"}},{"description":"# Tool discovery\n\nSearches over deferred tool metadata with BM25 and exposes matching tools for the next model call.\n\nSome of the tools, such as tools of MCP servers, may not have been provided to you upfront, and you should use this tool (`tool_search`) to search for the required tools. For MCP tool discovery, always use `tool_search`.","name":"tool_search","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of tools to return. Defaults to 8.","type":"number"},"query":{"description":"Search query for deferred tools.","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},{"description":"Search the authorized Skill metadata directory, including items outside the default View. Returns Skill refs for read or notion_use; it does not load instructions or activate workflows. For named Notion Skill existence or availability questions, set query to the name and refresh:true, even when already listed or previously absent. Answer existence and stated-purpose questions from metadata; read or use the Skill only when the user asks to inspect or apply its instructions. Also refresh after writes or to request the latest directory; selected Skill versions stay fixed. Report matching availability. Only fresh online results with exhaustive coverage and no failures establish that no available match was found in the searched scope; stale, offline, failed or partial results cannot establish current absence.\n\nCodemode: `tools.notion_list(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"notion_list","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Copy next_cursor to continue the same query and metadata publication; restart after refresh.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum metadata entries, default 20.","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"A short name or description keyword; empty lists the directory.","type":"string"},"refresh":{"description":"Refresh metadata for source, or all configured Notion sources when source is omitted. Keeps task pins; configured offline sources remain offline. Cannot combine with cursor.","type":"boolean"},"source":{"description":"Optional configured source ID to disambiguate directories.","type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"description":"Load task roots directly to apply their instructions; no preliminary read is needed. Requires load automatically: do not add them as independent roots unless independently requested. To introduce, summarize or inspect a Skill, use read instead. Copy a supplied ref, or pass task roots together. Use refresh:true only for a requested update; the supplied current or fixed main ref locates the same owner's latest version. Refresh roots with conflicting shared Requires together. Members remain candidates. Loading does not authorize executing a workflow. Notion consumption does not write to Notion.","name":"notion_use","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":64,"minItems":1,"type":"array"}],"description":"Supplied sr:C/sr:S or skill://<name-or-id>/<main> refs, or exact Notion Skill page URLs for task roots. Requires are included automatically. Prefer returned canonical refs for later actions."},"refresh":{"description":"Explicitly adopt current versions for only these roots after a complete successful load. Existing Requires-only nodes cannot become independent roots through refresh; explicitly use them without refresh first. Accepts the supplied sr:C/sr:S or main ref unchanged, for example {ref:[REF_A,REF_B],refresh:true} for shared roots. Failure keeps the previous selection.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}}]},"type":"message_start"},"episode_id":"standing-pilot80-run-1-four-auto-business-pilot80-037","monotonic_ns":"210712246344083","request_id":null,"run_id":"standing-pilot80-run-1-four-